<Project>

  <!--
    Developer tools: copy this file to `Directory.Build.local.props` (same folder, drop the `.example`)
    and rebuild. That copy is git-ignored and CI refuses a commit that contains it, because it is the
    only route by which a published build could carry developer surfaces.

    What the symbol adds:
      * a wrench button in the status window's title bar, opening the diagnostics window;
      * the live "gearset identity" panel in that window — server state, cached rows, and the uid plus
        the matched_by rung per gearset.

    What it does not change: the log itself, and `/xivarsenal gearsets`. A player's problem has to stay
    diagnosable in a released build, so the log and the chat dump are there for everyone. Only the
    interactive developer surface is absent.

    Verify it worked, from the repository root:
      dotnet build -c Release
      grep -c GearsetIdentityPanel src/EorzeaArsenalPlugin/bin/Release/EorzeaArsenalPlugin.dll
    One or more with this file in place, zero without it. Checking the built assembly rather than the
    source is the only check that actually answers the question.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <DefineConstants>$(DefineConstants);EORZEA_ARSENAL_DEVTOOLS</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
